{"id": 35, "ts": 1781168972.263432, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I concur with James and Sarah that Candidate\u202fC remains the strongest overall fit. Sarah has confirmed that C demonstrates calmness in crises, giving us solid evidence of stress resilience\u2014a critical safety criterion. While we lack direct observations of C\u2019s adaptability, the only note we have\u2014that he is not very willing to further his education\u2014suggests limited openness to development, but it does not outweigh his proven 100\u202f% reliability, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and the positive crew atmosphere he creates. In contrast, Candidate\u202fA, despite technical foresight and leadership, has no evidence of operational reliability, stress handling, or crew cooperation, and is described as unfriendly and unhealthy. Candidate\u202fB, though conscientious and stress\u2011resilient, is repeatedly noted as pretentious, uncooperative, and sometimes uses the wrong tone, raising serious crew\u2011cooperation concerns. Candidate\u202fD shows strong problem\u2011solving and responsibility, yet his moody, loner demeanor and lack of any crew\u2011cooperation evidence pose a risk for long\u2011haul cockpit dynamics. Given the current evidence, Candidate\u202fC\u2019s strengths on the core safety criteria outweigh the manageable communication and adaptability concerns."}
